WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.260
From more murderous games we never got to
see, to alternate costumes, characters, and

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.090
casting, Squid Game was almost completely
different!

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:12.740
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan, and
in this video I'm revealing everything that

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.290
was deleted, cut or changed in the final version
of Squid Game.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.869
Obviously, spoilers ahead, so take care.

00:00:18.869 --> 00:00:23.630
When the show's creator first came up with
the concept for Squid Game back in 2008, he

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:26.630
wanted to make a feature-length movie, not
a TV series.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:31.519
The original script was for a two-hour film
and although it mainly concentrated on the

00:00:31.519 --> 00:00:35.210
games, rather than the relationships between
characters and their backstories, there still

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:38.579
wasn't enough screen-time to cover all the
games we see in the show today.

00:00:38.579 --> 00:00:42.620
In fact, even when it came to the Netflix
series, there were still a whole bunch of

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:47.079
Korean children's games they considered including
but that ended up getting the chop.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:51.230
For instance, there was Gonggi, which consists
of throwing into the air, catching, and picking

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:52.859
up pebbles or other small objects.

00:00:52.859 --> 00:00:57.359
Not only is it popular in Korea, but it's
also found in countries around the world,

00:00:57.359 --> 00:01:00.890
under a variety of names including knucklebones
or jacks.

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:05.030
Another game the creator almost included but
decided to cut was a game based on a Korean

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:09.800
nursery rhyme that's similar to Oranges And
Lemons or London Bridge Is Falling Down, where

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:14.530
children form arches or gates with their arms
which they drop to catch players walking underneath

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:15.530
as the song finishes.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:19.450
I can imagine the horrific twist that the
show might have added to this game, given

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:23.730
how the nursery rhyme ending of Oranges and
Lemons is a chopper coming to chop off your

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:24.730
head.

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:29.410
A team game that almost made it into the series
was "Why Did You Come To My House?", where

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:33.210
players hold hands in two lines and advance
on each other, trying to win players from

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:35.280
the other side over to their own.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:40.150
It's a bit like the game Red Rover but the
Korean version also involves a song and Rock

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:41.400
Paper Scissors.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:46.090
Originally, instead of the red and blue tile
game the Salesman plays with Gi-hun, the show's

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:50.700
creator thought they should play a kind of
knitting game called "Cat's Cradle".

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:54.700
It's a game where players create string figures
between their fingers and he thought it would

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:57.040
be funny to see two men doing that.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.910
However, he said he gave up on the idea as
"the rules [wouldn't] be understood globally".

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:06.023
Elastics or Jump Rope was also suggested,
but he felt that didn't work "in terms of

00:02:06.023 --> 00:02:10.940
excitement and tension" and "was a little
difficult for everyone" when it came to explaining

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.160
all the rules.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.611
By the way, Gonggi and Elastics did at least
get a shout-out in the show when Gi-hun was

00:02:16.611 --> 00:02:19.890
speculating what game they might play next.

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:25.000
The distinctive costumes worn by the characters
are a crucial part of the highly stylised

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.000
series.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.170
But, originally, its creator wanted a completely
different look for the games' workers which

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:32.819
would have given them more of a Boy Scout
vibe.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:37.550
Now, I can see where he was coming from with
that idea as boy scouts are associated with

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:42.690
childhood and the whole show from its games
to its sets emphasises the irony of grown-ups

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:46.060
playing kids' games but with very adult consequences.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:50.060
However, Scout outfits wouldn't have given
the workers the same degree of anonymity.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:54.460
And they also wouldn't have given them the
sense of being "ants in an ant colony" that

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:56.230
the director was looking for.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:00.830
The show's art director also went through
numerous takes on the workers' masks, including

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:05.870
animal designs, before arriving at the final
fencing-inspired mask with lines reminiscent

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.300
of an ant's face.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:12.670
The ultimate design of hot-pink hooded jumpsuits
with black masks has proven hugely popular

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:16.960
around the world, with store-bought versions
selling like hot cakes, or should that be

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:17.960
honeycombs?

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.990
And becoming a top choice for Halloween.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:24.470
Some of the most heart-breaking moments in
the marbles game were originally going to

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.740
be very different.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:30.080
In the early days of Squid Game's development
as a movie, Ji-yeong as we know her didn't

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:34.490
exist and, rather than a young woman who'd
been imprisoned for killing her abusive father,

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:36.630
in her place was a male character.

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:41.120
However, ten years later, when writer-director
Hwang Dong-hyuk came to adapt his original

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.980
idea for TV,
he decided to create a female character instead

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:49.959
as he wanted to develop a bond between her
and North Korean defector Sae-byeok, and highlight

00:03:49.959 --> 00:03:54.340
two people who weren't fighting and killing
each other to climb up despite their gut-wrenching

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.330
life-or-death situation.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:59.720
The scenes between Ji-yeong and her partner
in the marbles game, with all their empathy

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:04.340
and understanding, are among the most powerful
and touching moments in the series and have

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:06.330
had viewers the world over in tears.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:10.850
In fact, just reading the script for that
episode had the actress who played Sae-byeok

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.319
sobbing her heart out.

00:04:12.319 --> 00:04:17.099
And as far as the show's creator is concerned,
those two characters are, in a way, the 'most

00:04:17.099 --> 00:04:22.279
innocent people' and Ji-yeong sacrificing
herself so Sae-byeok can reunite her family

00:04:22.279 --> 00:04:25.449
is the 'scene that makes you cry the most'.

00:04:25.449 --> 00:04:29.949
Another fan favourite performance we almost
missed out on was Anupam Tripathi's portrayal

00:04:29.949 --> 00:04:34.689
of Pakistani migrant worker Ali Abdul, who
ends up in the games as he can't support his

00:04:34.689 --> 00:04:38.319
family after his boss repeatedly refuses to
pay his wages.

00:04:38.319 --> 00:04:43.060
Although Ali is played beautifully by Tripathi,
apparently he wasn't the original choice for

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.060
the role.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:48.680
That was actually Filipino actor Carlo Aquino,
who the show's creator invited to audition

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:51.150
after seeing him in a Filipino movie.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:56.210
But despite being offered the part of Ali,
sadly for Aquino, Covid-19 restrictions prevented

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:58.270
him from travelling to Korea for the shoot.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:02.539
So, the production looked to foreign performers
already in the country which is how Indian

00:05:02.539 --> 00:05:06.699
actor Tripathi, who moved there 11 years ago,
got his chance to impress the team with his

00:05:06.699 --> 00:05:09.509
'emotional acting' and fluency in Korean.

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:13.319
Three auditions later, Tripathi got his big
breakthrough and went on to capture the hearts

00:05:13.319 --> 00:05:17.479
of millions with his take on the kind and
selfless Ali, leaving many of us in crying

00:05:17.479 --> 00:05:20.599
our eyes out during his heart-rending final
scenes.

00:05:20.599 --> 00:05:24.879
By the way, another Filipino actor Christian
Lagahit also auditioned for Ali, but while

00:05:24.879 --> 00:05:28.509
his acting was good, they were worried he
wasn't fluent enough in Korean.

00:05:28.509 --> 00:05:33.309
He did still end up in the show though, as
Player 276, who you can spot taking part in

00:05:33.309 --> 00:05:35.809
the tug-of-war on Gi-hun's team.

00:05:35.809 --> 00:05:40.470
As if having to play and win kids' game to
stay alive wasn't bad enough, the players

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:45.430
also have to contend with the murderous bully
Deok-su, and his gang including con-artist

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:50.139
Mi-nyeo, who interestingly enough weren't
in the original script for Squid Game.

00:05:50.139 --> 00:05:54.400
According to the show's creator, he added
them to the Netflix series as he wanted "a

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.389
villain character to escalate conflict".

00:05:57.389 --> 00:06:02.059
In the initial movie script, there was no
sign of policeman Jun-ho who, in the series,

00:06:02.059 --> 00:06:05.770
poses as a worker to infiltrate the games
and find his missing brother.

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:10.550
Jun-ho ends up being a crucial part of the
story as he gives viewers a backstage pass

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:13.469
to life behind the scenes for both the workers
and the VIPs.

00:06:13.469 --> 00:06:17.789
Thank goodness, then, that the show's creator
was able to add his character and storyline

00:06:17.789 --> 00:06:23.430
once he had lots of extra screen-time to play
with adapting his film idea for TV.

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:27.979
Combined with its eye-catching artwork, Squid
Game is such an attention-grabbing title for

00:06:27.979 --> 00:06:32.199
the show that it's hard to imagine anyone
ever thinking of calling it anything else!

00:06:32.199 --> 00:06:36.930
But in 2019, when Netflix first announced
they were producing the series, it had a totally

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:38.029
different name.

00:06:38.029 --> 00:06:41.720
Back then, it was called 'Round Six', after
the number of games played.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:45.080
According to Minyoung Kim, the Netflix executive
for the region,

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:49.349
that name came about because they wanted the
show to appeal to audiences everywhere and

00:06:49.349 --> 00:06:52.240
"were worried" not enough people would get
the title 'Squid Game'

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:56.090
What an odd name
as even in Korea, where it's a real children's

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:59.699
game, apparently it's not well-known to every
generation.

00:06:59.699 --> 00:07:04.399
So, initially, they thought the more general
name 'Round Six' would help people understand

00:07:04.399 --> 00:07:06.009
what the series was about.

00:07:06.009 --> 00:07:10.930
Fortunately, the writer-director later steered
them back to his original title as "it's a

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:14.250
unique show and [that] game is the essence
[of it]".

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:17.979
Even worse than a title change for many people
though, would have been if the show had never

00:07:17.979 --> 00:07:18.979
been made!

00:07:18.979 --> 00:07:24.180
And, for a long time, that was a very real
probability as all the Korean studios that

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:30.120
creator Hwang pitched his idea to, back in
2008/09, thought the whole concept was "too

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:31.669
grotesque and unrealistic".

00:07:31.669 --> 00:07:36.830
So, finding investors and actors for his script,
which at the time was for a two-hour movie,

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:38.280
proved impossible.

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:41.180
A decade later, however, the show's writer-director
says that,

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:45.669
"sadly, the world has changed [into a place]
where such an unbelievable survival story

00:07:45.669 --> 00:07:48.340
fits well",
and he added that some elements even seem

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:53.289
realistic now given so many people are interested
in fast money-making schemes, and [on top

00:07:53.289 --> 00:07:57.610
of] that, the pandemic has "exacerbated the
disparity between rich and poor".

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:03.150
In fact, he actually came up with the original
idea, after the global financial crisis of

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:07.879
2008, when three generations of his own family
were struggling for money and living on loans

00:08:07.879 --> 00:08:11.659
after his mother retired and a film he was
working on fell through.

00:08:11.659 --> 00:08:15.440
Indeed, things were so bad that at one point
"he had to stop writing the script" as he

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:17.559
needed to sell his laptop for cash.

00:08:17.559 --> 00:08:23.120
A breakthrough came, though, in 2018 when
he took his idea to Netflix who'd just recently

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:27.840
opened an office in Seoul and they snapped
up the project, suggesting they "[work] together

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:31.969
to turn it into a series", as they felt there
was much more to the story than could be contained

00:08:31.969 --> 00:08:32.969
in one movie.

00:08:32.969 --> 00:08:38.409
A lot of hard work later and Squid Game became
South Korea's first series to reach Netflix's

00:08:38.409 --> 00:08:41.130
number one spot in the US and around the world.

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:46.170
And the show's just full of incredible details
in the set design plus tons of sneaky easter

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:50.540
eggs and foreshadowing for all the characters,
which I discuss in lots more depth in my Things

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:51.540
You Missed video.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:54.589
Tap here to watch that or follow the link
in the video description.

00:08:54.589 --> 00:08:59.400
So, are there any games or things you'd like
to see in Season 2 of Squid Game?

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.339
Let me know in the comments below.

00:09:01.339 --> 00:09:05.000
And if you enjoyed this, then a thumbs-up
and a share are hugely appreciated.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:10.190
Tap left for my full Squid Game playlist including
amazing improvised moments that changed the

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:11.190
show.

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:12.660
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:14.069
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

